What does this print? Write the letters in order, separated by spaces.

```javascript
console.log("a");
setTimeout(() => console.log("b"), 0);
Promise.resolve().then(() => console.log("c"));
console.log("d");
```

This runs as an ES module. What does it print?

```javascript
async function f() {
  return 5;
}
const r = f();
console.log(r instanceof Promise, await r);
```

`delay(ms)` returns a promise that fulfils after `ms` milliseconds. Running

```javascript
await delay(100);
await delay(200);
await delay(300);
```

takes about 600 ms. To the nearest 100 ms, how long does this take instead?

```javascript
await Promise.all([delay(100), delay(200), delay(300)]);
```

What number does this print?

```javascript
const r = await Promise.reject(new Error("x"))
  .catch(() => 1)
  .then((v) => v + 1)
  .finally(() => 100);
console.log(r);
```

What does this print? Write both lines on one line, separated by a space.

```javascript
const delay = (ms) => new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, ms));
const done = [];
[30, 10, 20].forEach(async (ms) => {
  await delay(ms);
  done.push(ms);
});
console.log(done.length);
await delay(50);
console.log(done.join(" "));
```
